"id":"quartic.lemma-5","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 5","locator":"Lemma 5, Section 5.3","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 5** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Lemma 4.1); @Shaltiel2003; @Drucker2012). *Let $P$ be a partial function and $\\mu$ a distribution on its domain such that every deterministic algorithm making at most $L$ queries computes $P$ under $\\mu$ with probability at most $\\beta$. If $U_1,\\ldots,U_r$ are independent samples from $\\mu$, every algorithm making at most $L$ queries to each $U_h$ outputs $(P(U_1),\\ldots,P(U_r))$ with probability at most $\\beta^r$. The algorithm may be randomized, interleave its queries adaptively among the $r$ inputs, and receive additional information independent of $(U_1,\\ldots,U_r)$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-5","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-5","id":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/edges/%5B%22quartic.lemma-5%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.direct_product_average%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/edges/%5B%22quartic.lemma-5%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.direct_product_average%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/lean.QuarticQuery.direct_product_average"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.lemma-5","id":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/edges/%5B%22quartic.lemma-5%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.direct_product_randomized%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb2955